{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:FluidDynamics.TownsendBiotSavartStrain","@type":"LeanModule","name":"FluidDynamics.TownsendBiotSavartStrain","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Log.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Pow.Asymptotics","lean:module:Mathlib.Topology.Order.Basic"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.TownsendBiotSavart.kappa_squared_tends_to_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.TownsendBiotSavart.kappa_squared_tends_to_zero","kind":"theorem","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/townsend-biot-savart-strain.lean#L123-L207","doc":"**First-order flattening limit.**  Under the singular Biot–Savart strain,\nthe squared core aspect ratio vanishes at the collision:\n`κ²(τ) → 0` as `τ → 0⁺`.\n\nThe closed form `kappa_squared_closed_form` reduces the claim to the\nstandard real-analysis fact `τ² log τ → 0`.  See Townsend §IV and\nSaffman §11.2 for the textbook treatment.\n\n**Now proved, and the surrounding scaffolding was stale.**  Two docstrings\nstood here.  The first said \"the full chain of filter lemmas is mechanical\nbut tangential\"; the second announced an \"**External theorem (§3b-cond\npattern)** … auto-extracted from the single-sorry theorem body … pending\nMathlib infrastructure\", on a declaration named `..._axiom` that a\n*projecting wrapper* `kappa_squared_tends_to_zero` then consumed.\n\nNone of that was true by the time it was read: the declaration was already\na `theorem`, not an `axiom`, and its body was a real (broken) filter proof.\nThe seven errors were Mathlib API drift, not missing infrastructure —\n`Tendsto.pow` landing in `𝓝 (0^2)`, an rpow/natural-power mismatch, a\n`Pi.div` versus pointwise-division mismatch, and an implicit argument\npassed explicitly.  Repaired, the wrapper collapsed into this theorem, and\nthe `_axiom` suffix dropped: nothing outside this file referenced it, and\n`#print axioms` gives `[propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.TownsendBiotSavart.denominator_pos_near_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.TownsendBiotSavart.denominator_pos_near_zero","kind":"theorem","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/townsend-biot-savart-strain.lean#L103-L121","doc":"Helper: the limiting denominator $C_1 - \\nu\\tau^2$ is positive\nnear the collision for $C_1 > 0$. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.TownsendBiotSavart.kappa_squared_closed_form","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.TownsendBiotSavart.kappa_squared_closed_form","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/townsend-biot-savart-strain.lean#L93-L101","doc":"Closed form for the squared core aspect ratio\n$\\kappa^2(\\tau) = V_2(\\tau)/V_1(\\tau)$, factored to expose the\n$\\tau^2$ smallness at the collision. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.TownsendBiotSavart.V2_satisfies_ODE","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.TownsendBiotSavart.V2_satisfies_ODE","kind":"theorem","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/townsend-biot-savart-strain.lean#L86-L91","doc":"**ODE-2 holds algebraically.**  The pair `(V2, V2')` satisfies\n$\\tau\\,V_2' - V_2 = -2\\nu\\tau$. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.TownsendBiotSavart.V1_satisfies_ODE","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.TownsendBiotSavart.V1_satisfies_ODE","kind":"theorem","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/townsend-biot-savart-strain.lean#L78-L84","doc":"**ODE-1 holds algebraically.**  The pair `(V1, V1')` satisfies\n$\\tau\\,V_1' + V_1 = -2\\nu\\tau$. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.TownsendBiotSavart.V2'","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.TownsendBiotSavart.V2'","kind":"def","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/townsend-biot-savart-strain.lean#L73-L76","doc":"Formal derivative of `V2` w.r.t. $\\tau$:\n$V_2'(\\tau) = -2\\nu\\ln\\tau - 2\\nu + C_2$. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.TownsendBiotSavart.V2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.TownsendBiotSavart.V2","kind":"def","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/townsend-biot-savart-strain.lean#L68-L71","doc":"Candidate solution along the compressing axis,\n$V_2(\\tau) = -2\\nu\\tau\\ln\\tau + C_2\\,\\tau$. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.TownsendBiotSavart.V1'","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.TownsendBiotSavart.V1'","kind":"def","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/townsend-biot-savart-strain.lean#L64-L66","doc":"Formal derivative of `V1` w.r.t. $\\tau$:\n$V_1'(\\tau) = -C_1/\\tau^2 - \\nu$. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.TownsendBiotSavart.V1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.TownsendBiotSavart.V1","kind":"def","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/townsend-biot-savart-strain.lean#L60-L62","doc":"Candidate solution along the stretching axis,\n$V_1(\\tau) = C_1/\\tau - \\nu\\tau$. ","signatureChunk":0}]}